message: "If you use or reference this reverse-engineering research, architectural specifications, or telemetry datasets, please cite it as below."
title: "Active Theory WebGL & GPGPU Engine: 1:1 Architectural Reverse Engineering & Systems Dissection"
abstract: "An end-to-end academic reverse engineering, systems architecture specification, and empirical runtime telemetry study of the proprietary Active Theory WebGL/WebAudio engine (Hydra, Medusa, GLUI, Antimatter, Nuke). Documents zero-allocation memory pipelines, GPGPU particle physics, continuous procedural noise, Eulerian fluid dynamics, and driver-level shader pre-warming."
